WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.920
The original Neuropixels probe carries 960 recording sites.

2
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.680
Does it record 960 neurons?

3
00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:22.963
Not necessarily. The original probe reads out only 384 sites at a time.

4
00:00:23.803 --> 00:00:25.203
Each one read out is a channel.

5
00:00:26.233 --> 00:00:28.833
And neurons are not read off sites at all.

6
00:00:29.873 --> 00:00:31.353
Software sorts the spikes into units.

7
00:00:32.153 --> 00:00:34.393
It can find more units than channels, or fewer.

8
00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:38.207
One neuron shows up on several neighbouring sites.

9
00:00:38.207 --> 00:00:40.427
One site hears several neurons.

10
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:44.450
So a unit can merge two neurons, or split one.

11
00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.610
Treat each unit as an inference, with quality scores.

12
00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:49.810
Notice the ladder.

13
00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:53.070
Sites, then channels, then units, then neurons.

14
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:55.710
Each rung is a step from what you want.

15
00:00:56.683 --> 00:00:58.903
Calcium imaging has a ladder too.

16
00:00:59.763 --> 00:01:03.083
A spike lets calcium in, and calcium makes a sensor glow.

17
00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:08.513
The glow is real, but it lags and blurs the spike, like steam from a kettle.

18
00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.607
An atlas sorts cells into clusters.

19
00:01:14.587 --> 00:01:16.127
Is each cluster a true cell type?

20
00:01:16.987 --> 00:01:18.067
Not every one may be.

21
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.700
A connectome counts synapses.

22
00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:22.620
Is a count a strength?

23
00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.920
Treating it as one is an assumption, not a measurement.

24
00:01:26.983 --> 00:01:28.923
Even a pile of units has a step.

25
00:01:29.863 --> 00:01:31.383
Units from one mouse share that mouse.

26
00:01:32.383 --> 00:01:33.943
So here is the one idea.

27
00:01:34.863 --> 00:01:38.383
Each of these numbers is a proxy, one or more steps from your claim.

28
00:01:39.417 --> 00:01:44.477
Name each step. Trust it only as far as someone has measured that step, in

29
00:01:44.477 --> 00:01:45.537
conditions like yours.

30
00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:49.447
More cells sharpen the estimate for each animal.

31
00:01:50.187 --> 00:01:52.087
But they never count as more animals.

32
00:01:53.117 --> 00:01:57.497
Every method has a row like this: the number it gives, and the step to your claim.

33
00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:00.830
The rule says how far to trust a measurement.

34
00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:03.370
It cannot show a pathway is needed.

35
00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.210
That takes a manipulation.

36
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:11.340
The next two films follow two of these steps closely: light to spikes, and cells to

37
00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:11.540
mice.
